{"id": "data/normal/4618", "subject": "● Siemens Internship Opportunity", "body": "Position Description:\nResearch Intern for Software Testing Quality &amp; Process Modeling\nThe position will involve in the research project of measuring quality of testing, which is jointly sponsored by Siemens Corporate Technology and COM MN. This study aims to provide advanced tools and technologies to support testing management and improve testing quality.\nThe successful completion of this project would lead to new views in software reliability engineering under Siemens environment. The first phase of the project mainly focuses on design and implementation of an innovative model used to predict residual defects and estimate the quality of system testing. \n \nRequirements:\n&amp;#8226;         Ph.D or M.S candidate in computer science.\n&amp;#8226;         Good English reading and writing skills.\n&amp;#8226;         Proficiency in at least one programming language (C/C++/Java)\n&amp;#8226;         Good understanding of software development process (e.g. CMM)\n&amp;#8226;         Experienced in conducting statistical analysis via mathematic / statistical tools (MatLab, MathCad, Mathematica, etc).\n&amp;#8226;         Experience and knowledge in mobile communication network is highly desirable.\n&amp;#8226;         Knowledge and experience in Excel VBA programming is highly desirable.\nAbility to work independently on the programming assignment, while interacting with the other researchers on design and experimentation.\nSend you resume to: internship.cn@siemens.com    before August\n\n", "from": "Tran Quang Anh <mei@cernet.edu.cn>", "attachments": [], "label": "ham"}
